counterfactuals.output:
1. A test system for testing a high-temperature fuel cell operated with a carbon-based combustible gas, the test system comprising:

at least one high-temperature fuel cell having an anode, a cathode, and an electrolyte disposed between the anode and the cathode;

a pair of interconnection plates arranged on opposite sides of the at least one high-temperature fuel cell;

a fuel-gas flow field formed between one of the interconnection plates and the anode, the fuel-gas flow field comprising fuel-gas flow channels configured to guide a carbon-based combustible gas along the anode;

an oxidizing-gas flow field formed between another of the interconnection plates and the cathode, the oxidizing-gas flow field comprising oxidizing-gas flow channels configured to guide an oxidizing gas along the cathode;

a fuel-gas supply line configured to supply the carbon-based combustible gas to the fuel-gas flow channels;

an oxidizing-gas supply line configured to supply the oxidizing gas to the oxidizing-gas flow channels;

a heating device configured to maintain the at least one high-temperature fuel cell at an operating temperature suitable for electrochemical conversion of the carbon-based combustible gas; and

a measurement arrangement electrically connected to the interconnection plates and configured to determine at least one operating parameter of the at least one high-temperature fuel cell during supply of the carbon-based combustible gas and the oxidizing gas.
